    "raw": "Given that Diana gets 30 minutes of video game time for every hour she reads, and her dad decided to raise her reward by 20%, we need to find out how many more minutes of video game time she will get as a result of this raise, given that Diana read for 12 hours this week.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the original reward:\n- Original reward per hour of reading: 30 minutes\n- Hours read: 12\n- Original total video game time: \\(30 \\text{ minutes/hour} \\times 12 \\text{ hours} = 360 \\text{ minutes}\\)\n\nNext, we calculate the new reward after the 20% increase:\n- Increase in reward: \\(30 \\text{ minutes} \\times 0.20 = 6 \\text{ minutes}\\)\n- New reward per hour: \\(30 \\text{ minutes} + 6 \\text{ minutes} = 36 \\text{ minutes}\\)\n\nNow, we calculate the new total video game time with the increased reward:\n- New total video game time: \\(36 \\text{ minutes/hour} \\times 12 \\text{ hours} = 432 \\text{ minutes}\\)\n\nTo find out how many more minutes of video game time she will get as a result of the raise, we subtract the original total from the new total:\n- Additional video game time: \\(432 \\text{ minutes} - 360 \\text{ minutes} = 72 \\text{ minutes}\\)\n\nThus, Diana will get 72 more minutes of video game time as a result of the raise.\n\nFINAL: 72",
